<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
<section>
  <div class="section-tag">How it works</div>
  <h2>From kernel event to blocked threat</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">
    OSEye observes your Linux endpoints at the kernel level, correlates events against detection rules and ML baselines, then acts — all without leaving your infrastructure.
  </p>
  <div class="how-grid">
    <div class="how-item">
      <div class="how-num">01 — Collect</div>
      <div class="how-icon" style="background:rgba(0,212,255,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#00d4ff" stroke-width="1.8"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="12" x2="15" y2="15"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="1" fill="#00d4ff"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="how-title">Kernel-level telemetry</div>
      <div class="how-desc">
        The Go agent instruments the Linux kernel via eBPF, auditd, fanotify, inotify, netlink and more.
        Every syscall, file access, network connection and process spawn is captured — in real time, at near-zero cost.
      </div>
      <div class="how-tags">
        <span class="tag">eBPF</span><span class="tag">auditd</span>
        <span class="tag">fanotify</span><span class="tag">procfs</span>
        <span class="tag">netlink</span><span class="tag">journald</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="how-item">
      <div class="how-num">02 — Detect</div>
      <div class="how-icon" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.8"><polygon points="12 2 15.09 8.26 22 9.27 17 14.14 18.18 21.02 12 17.77 5.82 21.02 7 14.14 2 9.27 8.91 8.26 12 2"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="how-title">Multi-layer detection</div>
      <div class="how-desc">
        Events stream to the server where three detection engines run in parallel: 35+ YAML rules mapped to MITRE ATT&CK,
        online ML anomaly detection per entity (HalfSpaceTrees), and threat intelligence enrichment (AbuseIPDB, VirusTotal, MISP).
      </div>
      <div class="how-tags">
        <span class="tag">YAML rules</span><span class="tag">ML baseline</span>
        <span class="tag">MITRE ATT&CK</span><span class="tag">TI enrichment</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="how-item">
      <div class="how-num">03 — Respond</div>
      <div class="how-icon" style="background:rgba(74,222,128,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.8"><polyline points="9 11 12 14 22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h11"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="how-title">Autonomous response</div>
      <div class="how-desc">
        Confirmed threats trigger immediate response actions: kill process, block IP via nftables, quarantine file.
        All actions are logged to an immutable BLAKE3 audit journal. Analysts can review and roll back from the dashboard.
      </div>
      <div class="how-tags">
        <span class="tag">kill PID</span><span class="tag">nftables block</span>
        <span class="tag">file quarantine</span><span class="tag">audit journal</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FEATURES -->
<section style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="section-tag">Capabilities</div>
  <h2>Everything a security team needs</h2>
  <p class="section-sub">
    Built from the ground up for Linux. Designed to be self-hosted, auditable, and extensible.
  </p>
  <div class="features-grid">

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon" style="background:rgba(0,212,255,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#00d4ff" stroke-width="1.8"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-title">eBPF-native agent</div>
      <div class="feature-desc">Single static Go binary, no runtime dependencies. Packages for .deb, .rpm, Docker, systemd. Offline-resilient with local SQLite buffer.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-title">35+ detection rules</div>
      <div class="feature-desc">YAML rules aligned to MITRE ATT&CK, hot-reloaded at runtime. Covers privilege escalation, lateral movement, persistence, data exfiltration and more.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon" style="background:rgba(74,222,128,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#4ade80" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M21 16V8a2 2 0 00-1-1.73l-7-4a2 2 0 00-2 0l-7 4A2 2 0 003 8v8a2 2 0 001 1.73l7 4a2 2 0 002 0l7-4A2 2 0 0021 16z"/><polyline points="3.27 6.96 12 12.01 20.73 6.96"/><line x1="12" y1="22.08" x2="12" y2="12"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-title">ML anomaly detection</div>
      <div class="feature-desc">Online HalfSpaceTrees per entity via River. Automatic baseline learning, MITRE classifier. Detects deviations without pre-labeled training data.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon" style="background:rgba(239,68,68,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="1.8"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="4.93" y1="4.93" x2="19.07" y2="19.07"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-title">Response engine</div>
      <div class="feature-desc">8 decision types, act-then-notify with admin rollback. Kill process, block IP via nftables, quarantine file. All actions recorded in an immutable BLAKE3 journal.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon" style="background:rgba(0,212,255,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#00d4ff" stroke-width="1.8"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0110 0v4"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-title">mTLS + RBAC</div>
      <div class="feature-desc">Agent-to-server mutual TLS with rotating certificates. Role-based access control with analyst and admin profiles. Ed25519-signed plugin manifests.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-icon" style="background:rgba(245,158,11,.08)">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M20.59 13.41l-7.17 7.17a2 2 0 01-2.83 0L2 12V2h10l8.59 8.59a2 2 0 010 2.82z"/><line x1="7" y1="7" x2="7.01" y2="7"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-title">Plugin SDK</div>
      <div class="feature-desc">Python extensions — Analyzer, Exporter, Collector — sandboxed over a Unix IPC socket. Ship your own detectors or export events to SIEM, SOAR, Slack.</div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

